From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:05:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 53/58] serve: STRATA_ADMIT_SHORT_FIRST=<tokens> admits short
 prompts before long ones (opt-in)

New requests took the control lines in whatever order the lock fell, so a 500-token chat question could wait
behind several agent reads. With the env, a prompt of at most that many tokens goes first (arrival order within
each class); a longer one that waited STRATA_ADMIT_MAX_WAIT_S (30 s) counts as short. A request already in
acquire() gives the lines back when a shorter one came. Only the order changes, never what is read.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
